cf. issues/closed/windows-msys-paths-in-autolisp-load.issue

The fix works in clautolisp, but not in alfe --clautolisp:

How come we get a different behavior between alfe --clautolisp and clautolisp ?
In general we should get strictly the same semantics, unless an exception is specified and documented.


In alfe, the msys path IS NOT resoved to windows, hence the could not locate error:

/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms
feat-eamoa-24679-pb-tests-cad-migration-sigfic
09:10[COMMUN+PPBN02261@PF5S26BT w32 schms 40G]$ TRUSTEDPATHS="$trusted_paths" \
OUTFILE="/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.out" \
ERRFILE="/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.err" \
STATUSFILE="/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.status" \
            alfe -norc --clautolisp --host cador --dialect bricscad-v26 --timeout 120 -Esource WINDOWS-1252 --on-error debug \
            -x '(setq *AUTOLISP_OUTFILE* "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.out")' \
            -x '(setq *AUTOLISP_ERRFILE* "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.err")' \
            -x '(setq *AUTOLISP_STATUSFILE* "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire/test-unitaire.status")' \
            -x '(setq *AUTOLISP_WORKDIR* "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/.autolisp-workdir/unitaire")' \
            -x '(setq *tu:self-override* "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/test-unitaire.lsp")'  -i
> > > > > > > > > alfe> (load "/c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/test-unitaire.lsp")

; runtime error: LOAD-FILE-NOT-FOUND: LOAD could not locate /c/Users/PPBN02261/works/sncf-reseau/src/schms/tests/test-unitaire.lsp.
alfe> (quit)



While in clautolisp, the msys path IS resoved to windows path, and loading the file works:


